WEBVTT

00:00.700 --> 00:04.190
I can't understand why you feel this way!

00:04.190 --> 00:07.260
How can you say that you 
love Masamune-sama, then?

00:09.060 --> 00:10.190
Did you know?

00:11.030 --> 00:14.610
He used to be a bit weird and different, too.

00:15.120 --> 00:19.830
Even if he dislikes me or denies me, 
I won't let Masamune go now.

00:20.590 --> 00:21.790
Because...

00:22.430 --> 00:23.750
that's just who I am.

00:25.130 --> 00:29.460
So... I'm in the same boat as you. 
Our feelings only go one way.

00:34.090 --> 00:37.250
I think my feelings might be 
more deeply rooted, though.

01:03.310 --> 01:04.570
Man, it's cold.

02:35.050 --> 02:40.970
<b>#10 "Whiteout"</b>

02:42.430 --> 02:43.450
Yoshino.

02:45.450 --> 02:46.770
Sorry to keep you waiting.

02:47.090 --> 02:49.330
It's cold, so let's get something to eat.

02:50.980 --> 02:54.690
A café, a family restaurant, or a 
sweets parlor? Where should we go?

02:56.820 --> 02:57.970
Aki-sama...

02:57.970 --> 02:59.630
Has something happened?

03:00.910 --> 03:02.730
Not really.

03:02.730 --> 03:04.070
You're lying.

03:10.750 --> 03:13.690
I just had a little conversation.

03:13.690 --> 03:16.340
I was told that Makabe doesn't 
really have feelings for me,

03:16.340 --> 03:18.870
and that I should break up with him... 
by Commando girl.

03:20.630 --> 03:22.360
Stop that, Yoshino!

03:22.360 --> 03:25.210
But Aki-sama, that's so cruel!

03:37.520 --> 03:41.060
What she said wasn't exactly wrong, though.

03:41.580 --> 03:44.450
It's true that he doesn't love me.

03:45.510 --> 03:49.630
He only got close to me because he hates me.

03:50.290 --> 03:51.460
No...

03:51.870 --> 03:53.920
That's not true, Aki-sama!

03:54.450 --> 03:55.740
Yoshino?

03:55.760 --> 03:58.380
You've completely got the wrong idea.

03:58.970 --> 04:04.980
It's all my fault. I did this.

04:06.170 --> 04:07.460
I'm so sorry...

04:08.870 --> 04:11.140
You two aren't at fault here.

04:20.410 --> 04:21.490
I...

04:22.290 --> 04:27.010
hated Pig's Foot so much, and I didn't 
want him to take you from me...

04:27.980 --> 04:30.870
That's why I called him 
"Pig's Foot
 and chased him off.

04:31.980 --> 04:36.420
Apparently, Pig's Foot transferred 
to our school to get revenge.

04:36.930 --> 04:39.970
But I didn't want him to do that.

04:40.420 --> 04:45.590
That's why I pretended to help him, but I 
was going to try to help you two make up.

04:47.770 --> 04:49.850
So you worked really hard.

04:55.230 --> 04:57.570
Please don't say that he doesn't love you.

04:58.450 --> 05:01.180
The feelings between you 
and Pig's Foot are mutual.

05:01.610 --> 05:03.530
Pig's Foot knows that, too.

05:04.430 --> 05:07.170
<i>Oh, you're so...</i>

05:08.250 --> 05:11.350
<i>No. You two are so...</i>

05:14.950 --> 05:16.100
You'll get wet.

05:17.730 --> 05:21.590
Say, there's something 
I want you to look into.

05:24.790 --> 05:25.840
Whoa.

05:25.840 --> 05:27.760
It really piled up.

05:28.010 --> 05:29.600
Wow, that's amazing!

05:29.600 --> 05:32.220
It's been forever since we got this much snow!

05:32.220 --> 05:33.900
Let's make a snowman!

05:33.900 --> 05:35.020
Nope, not happening.

05:35.420 --> 05:36.950
Huh? Why not?

05:37.420 --> 05:40.090
It's cold, it's too much trouble, and it's cold.

05:40.090 --> 05:42.900
Boo. Fine, then. I'll make one myself.

05:43.260 --> 05:47.390
You just stay and sulk in the warm 
house, Grandpa Party Pooper.

05:47.390 --> 05:48.490
Grandpa?!

05:49.990 --> 05:51.980
Don't you dare underestimate my muscles!

05:51.980 --> 05:54.240
Hup, hup, hup, hup, hup, hup!

05:51.980 --> 05:54.240
Wow! That's the spirit, Onii-chan!

05:55.780 --> 05:57.460
Should we use buttons for its eyes?

05:57.780 --> 06:00.180
Wait, leave this to me.

06:03.100 --> 06:04.670
There, all done.

06:07.980 --> 06:11.180
Wait, wait, that's terrifying! 
Why is it a Daruma doll?!

06:11.180 --> 06:13.490
Well, a snowman is technically 
called "yukidaruma," right?

06:13.490 --> 06:14.470
Ah...

06:14.810 --> 06:18.230
It's good luck, too. This is one of my best.

06:18.700 --> 06:22.860
Huh... Who are you sending that to? 
Your girlfriend?

06:22.860 --> 06:24.570
Wh-Why does that matter?

06:24.890 --> 06:29.060
Hey, when are you going to let me 
meet this supposed girlfriend of yours?

06:29.060 --> 06:29.950
What?

06:29.950 --> 06:32.860
Mom said she wants to meet her, too.

06:32.860 --> 06:35.660
Oh! Why don't we invite her 
over this weekend?

06:35.660 --> 06:37.740
Huh?! No way!

06:37.740 --> 06:41.940
Boo... I just want to be friends 
with your girlfriend.

06:42.500 --> 06:45.210
Well, eventually...

06:45.500 --> 06:47.460
Really?! You better!

06:47.460 --> 06:49.310
Oh, jeez. All right already.

06:53.100 --> 06:55.390
White Day is next week.

06:55.390 --> 06:59.000
Man, I can't wait to get all those return gifts.

06:59.000 --> 07:00.570
Right?

07:01.350 --> 07:04.040
Man, every single year! That pressure!

07:04.040 --> 07:06.690
All because we accepted 
chocolates on Valentine's Day...

07:06.690 --> 07:07.820
Even if it was obligatory!

07:10.460 --> 07:12.500
Why did you do that?

07:13.870 --> 07:16.290
If I said it was for 
Masamune-sama's happiness...

07:16.870 --> 07:19.970
Would ya think I'm oversteppin' my bounds?

07:20.900 --> 07:21.500
Huh?

07:22.110 --> 07:27.460
Is being hurt, pushing yourself too hard, 
and lying to yourself really what love is?

07:28.700 --> 07:31.470
No one can attain happiness from that.

07:32.460 --> 07:34.890
That includes Aki-sama, of course.

07:35.250 --> 07:36.770
Fujinomiya-san...

07:37.390 --> 07:39.900
I don't really understand, but...

07:39.900 --> 07:44.020
To them, I'm sure I'm a villain.

07:44.730 --> 07:45.360
But...

07:46.350 --> 07:49.660
That's fine. That's perfectly fine.

07:57.570 --> 08:00.260
<i>I wonder why she wants to know about this...</i>

08:20.650 --> 08:23.930
Man, I'm full.

08:23.930 --> 08:25.960
I am, too. What a lovely meal.

08:25.960 --> 08:27.130
What, already?!

08:27.820 --> 08:31.940
W-Well, I was too hungry 
earlier, so I already ate...

08:32.290 --> 08:33.490
Oh, okay.

08:33.890 --> 08:38.120
Yeah, there's no way you'd be 
satisfied with just five breads.

08:38.120 --> 08:40.200
Oh, shut up!

08:40.490 --> 08:43.650
Oh, right. Did you see that 
photo I sent this morning?

08:43.650 --> 08:45.420
Oh, of the snowman?

08:45.760 --> 08:47.450
Didn't that look awesome?

08:47.900 --> 08:51.300
Ah... I just thought you had a lot of 
time on your hands in the morning.

08:51.300 --> 08:52.880
D'oh! That's so mean!

08:54.030 --> 08:57.730
I'm kidding. You must be 
really close to your little sister.

08:57.730 --> 08:59.140
Thanks for sending me this.

09:01.190 --> 09:04.600
So, hey... If you have time sometime...

09:06.750 --> 09:08.300
N-No, never mind!

09:08.300 --> 09:09.540
Don't worry about it!

09:09.540 --> 09:11.480
Oh, just spit it out already.

09:11.780 --> 09:13.990
I'll tell you some other time.

09:13.990 --> 09:17.410
Fine, I'll wait. But I won't get my hopes up.

09:23.490 --> 09:24.930
Fujinomiya-san!

09:27.850 --> 09:30.940
Kojuurou-sama, did you need something?

09:30.940 --> 09:33.090
U-Um...

09:33.090 --> 09:35.090
Why don't we walk home together?

09:48.150 --> 09:51.690
It's actually quite nice walking 
home every once in a while.

09:52.030 --> 09:55.650
O-Oh, right. You usually 
get a ride to and from school.

09:55.980 --> 09:58.200
Sorry to ask you to do this on short notice.

09:58.200 --> 09:59.660
It's perfectly fine.

10:05.080 --> 10:08.210
You can be much harsher 
with me if you'd like.

10:09.440 --> 10:13.850
Considering what I did, it wouldn't be 
unexpected for you to despise me.

10:13.850 --> 10:15.260
D-Despise you?!

10:15.730 --> 10:18.470
Don't say that! I'd never 
feel that way about you!

10:20.120 --> 10:22.350
Sure, I was a little surprised,

10:22.870 --> 10:25.890
but I was just worried about you.

10:27.810 --> 10:31.360
I still don't regret what I said to Aki-sama...

10:31.950 --> 10:35.690
But I'd be lying if I said 
that I didn't feel guilty.

10:35.690 --> 10:38.860
It doesn't appear as though Aki-sama 
and Masamune-sama have broken up,

10:38.860 --> 10:40.820
and part of me is relieved by that.

10:43.280 --> 10:46.110
I wonder what I really am.

10:47.220 --> 10:49.740
To me, Fujinomiya-san...

10:50.140 --> 10:52.710
You're a very straightforward 
and kind person.

10:57.650 --> 10:59.770
Aki-sama, it's Yoshino.

10:59.770 --> 11:00.630
Come in.

11:00.920 --> 11:03.300
I've finished looking into the 
thing you asked me about.

11:03.300 --> 11:05.850
Thanks. That must have been rough.

11:06.890 --> 11:08.210
Um...

11:08.210 --> 11:09.060
Yes?

11:09.700 --> 11:12.770
How have things been with
Pig's Foo—I mean, Makabe?

11:12.770 --> 11:16.270
What? Where did that come from?

11:16.270 --> 11:18.300
I-I'm sorry.

11:18.300 --> 11:22.300
It's all right. There's nothing 
for you to worry about.

11:22.730 --> 11:23.990
Aki-sama...

11:23.990 --> 11:30.430
Because you told me the truth, 
I don't have to doubt him anymore.

11:30.890 --> 11:34.710
And thanks to that, I can now 
face him with how I truly feel.

11:35.420 --> 11:36.930
Thanks, Yoshino.

11:42.740 --> 11:43.450
Adagaki Aki

11:44.620 --> 11:45.860
Adagaki-san?

11:47.890 --> 11:48.780
Hello?

11:48.780 --> 11:51.140
<i>Hey, Makabe? Is now a good time?</i>

11:51.140 --> 11:52.680
Sure. What's up?

11:52.680 --> 11:55.410
<i>Do you want to go on a date this weekend?</i>

11:56.210 --> 11:59.110
<i>A da— Adagaki-san is inviting me?!</i>

11:59.750 --> 12:03.510
Sure. I was actually about 
to ask you out on one, too.

12:04.010 --> 12:05.890
<i>Really? Great.</i>

12:06.290 --> 12:08.340
<i>White Day is coming up, too.</i>

12:08.340 --> 12:11.040
<i>Who?! Wha— White Day?!</i>

12:11.530 --> 12:13.850
<i>Oh, shit. I had nothing planned.</i>

12:14.540 --> 12:18.100
<i>Uh, wait. I'm... supposed to 
give her something back, right?</i>

12:18.100 --> 12:18.980
<i>What do I give her?</i>

12:18.980 --> 12:20.850
<i>Like, how much? 
What situation should this be?</i>

12:20.850 --> 12:23.510
<i>Also, Makabe... Are you listening?</i>

12:23.510 --> 12:26.440
I-I'm listening. Of course I'm listening.

12:26.220 --> 12:33.730
White Day what to return to top choice
 White Day girlfriend date
 White Day recommended shops
 White Day recommended presents

12:26.440 --> 12:27.780
<i>Okay, good.</i>

12:28.330 --> 12:32.100
<i>For this date, I'd like you 
to let me plan everything.</i>

12:32.100 --> 12:33.730
<i>There's somewhere I'd like to take you.</i>

12:34.090 --> 12:37.410
Ah... Yeah, sure. 
Did you want to go shopping?

12:37.410 --> 12:37.980
<i>Well,</i>

12:37.980 --> 12:39.230
something like that.

12:39.690 --> 12:41.990
<i>Yeah? That seems pretty fun.</i>

12:42.460 --> 12:43.750
Perhaps.

12:44.250 --> 12:46.160
<i>Okay, sounds good.</i>

12:46.160 --> 12:48.460
Yes. Goodnight.

12:48.970 --> 12:49.870
<i>Goodnight.</i>

12:57.930 --> 12:59.420
Let's see...

12:59.420 --> 13:01.630
Yeah, you should get her a ring.

13:01.630 --> 13:04.410
A ring?! For White Day?!

13:04.410 --> 13:07.300
Yeah! A ring would be great.

13:07.300 --> 13:08.090
Notion rejected!

13:08.090 --> 13:11.130
Aw, then how about 
an electric facial device?

13:11.130 --> 13:13.110
You just want one for yourself.

13:14.470 --> 13:17.310
<i>Nope, she's no help at all.</i>

13:18.100 --> 13:21.920
Well, since she gave you homemade 
chocolates for Valentine's Day,

13:21.920 --> 13:24.950
why don't you go all-out and 
make something for her, as well?

13:25.890 --> 13:26.790
Huh...

13:27.410 --> 13:31.870
Almond Powder

13:27.410 --> 13:31.870
Cake Flour

13:27.800 --> 13:31.870
Thirty-five grams of egg whites, 
thirty grams of granulated sugar,

13:32.140 --> 13:34.630
thirty-five grams of almond powder...

13:35.050 --> 13:36.670
What are you going to make?

13:36.670 --> 13:39.330
What else? Macarons, 
since girls like them so much.

13:39.330 --> 13:41.050
What? Really?

13:41.050 --> 13:44.050
Macarons are really hard to make. 
Are you sure about this?

13:44.050 --> 13:44.890
Yeah...

13:45.470 --> 13:48.930
Why not try something simpler, like cookies?

13:48.930 --> 13:49.930
Yeah, yeah...

13:50.940 --> 13:53.560
No, I'm going to make macarons.

13:53.560 --> 13:55.390
There's nothing that I can't do!

13:58.860 --> 14:00.380
Are macarons supposed to look like this?

14:00.750 --> 14:03.110
Nope. Not even close.

14:05.380 --> 14:06.260
How about this?

14:06.260 --> 14:08.030
Those are clearly just crackers.

14:11.050 --> 14:12.490
Well played, macarons...

14:12.850 --> 14:14.870
But I will not give up!

14:15.210 --> 14:16.080
Not ever!

14:16.080 --> 14:19.830
I'm going to... bake you up nice and round!

14:20.830 --> 14:24.460
So... you decided to just buy them.

14:24.460 --> 14:28.010
Yeah, I did. Do you know any good places?

14:28.340 --> 14:32.510
Well... What sweets does Adagaki-san like?

14:32.910 --> 14:35.450
Anything that tastes good.

14:37.040 --> 14:40.440
For better or for worse, 
Adagaki-san's got a sharp tongue.

14:40.770 --> 14:43.630
She won't be happy unless she gets the best.

14:43.630 --> 14:47.650
Hmm... Then I know the best place.

14:53.170 --> 14:54.240
What?

14:54.240 --> 14:55.540
So cute!

14:55.540 --> 14:56.700
Thank you.

14:56.700 --> 14:58.120
Thanks.

14:58.120 --> 15:00.240
Wow, this is crazy.

15:00.240 --> 15:02.330
I figured there'd be a lot of people.

15:02.820 --> 15:05.000
Why are there so many girls here?

15:05.000 --> 15:08.960
They're probably here for all the 
limited-edition White Day sweets.

15:08.960 --> 15:12.720
In some couples, the wife gives 
the return gift, not the husband.

15:13.010 --> 15:16.720
Wait, do you always shop at places like this?

15:16.720 --> 15:20.690
For a special treat every now 
and then. I love depachikas.

15:23.150 --> 15:25.110
Shortcake

15:23.150 --> 15:25.110
Éclair

15:23.150 --> 15:25.110
Chocolate Millefeuille

15:23.150 --> 15:25.110
Rare cheesecake

15:23.150 --> 15:25.110
Mocha Roll

15:23.150 --> 15:25.110
Millefeuille

15:23.570 --> 15:25.110
Wow!

15:25.110 --> 15:27.400
What a delicious-looking Mont Blanc!

15:27.400 --> 15:29.660
Oh, I guess this is pistachio cake.

15:29.660 --> 15:31.700
Yeah they do look really good.

15:31.700 --> 15:33.660
<b>Pistachio Cake</b>

15:32.170 --> 15:33.130
It's so expensive!

15:33.660 --> 15:36.580
That's standard for high-grade sweets.

15:36.580 --> 15:37.870
Seriously?

15:37.870 --> 15:40.540
Oh, since you're giving it to her 
in return for Valentine's Day,

15:40.540 --> 15:43.380
you might want to get something that'll keep.

15:43.380 --> 15:44.750
Like cookies or chocolates.

15:45.660 --> 15:49.140
There are so many. Which one should I get?

15:50.220 --> 15:53.180
<b>White
Day
Fair
Limited
Time
Shop</b>

15:53.180 --> 15:55.300
Limited time?

15:55.300 --> 15:57.640
Apparently, this shop is only here right now.

16:03.560 --> 16:04.800
So cute!

16:03.840 --> 16:05.740
Wow, they're so cute.

16:04.800 --> 16:06.520
They're great.

16:05.740 --> 16:06.520
Yeah.

16:06.520 --> 16:07.400
They are cute.

16:09.980 --> 16:13.410
It seems cheeky, sorta like Adagaki-san.

16:13.930 --> 16:16.620
Okay, I'll take it. May I get this, please?

16:21.810 --> 16:24.450
Thanks for everything today. 
You really helped.

16:24.450 --> 16:26.000
It's no big deal.

16:26.460 --> 16:29.170
I hope Adagaki-san likes it.

16:29.730 --> 16:30.510
Yeah.

16:32.190 --> 16:34.800
I see you bought some, too. Are they for you?

16:34.800 --> 16:35.890
Huh?

16:35.890 --> 16:39.640
N-No. I thought I'd give them to Fujinomiya-san.

16:39.930 --> 16:42.600
Huh? Even though you gave 
her a Valentine's Day gift?

16:43.020 --> 16:47.310
I did... But after looking at a few of these, 
I felt like giving her something.

16:47.710 --> 16:49.590
Well, I guess that's something you'd do.

16:50.650 --> 16:54.840
Oh, hey. Considering what time it is, 
why don't we get something to eat?

16:54.840 --> 16:57.080
Good idea. How about ramen?

16:57.080 --> 16:59.280
Ramen at night?

17:00.150 --> 17:02.520
That's so many calories, but I'll go with you.

17:02.520 --> 17:03.750
Yay!

17:16.550 --> 17:17.820
Are you going on a date?

17:18.250 --> 17:20.560
I see you're as sharp as usual.

17:21.140 --> 17:22.990
Enjoying your youth, I see.

17:26.310 --> 17:28.620
Well, I'll see you later.

17:28.620 --> 17:30.980
Yes. Have a wonderful time.

17:33.700 --> 17:36.950
You should enjoy your youth 
while you still can, too.

17:40.460 --> 17:43.950
Whatever. I'm not even interested in that.

17:50.110 --> 17:52.340
This is the place, right?

17:54.230 --> 17:55.610
Welcome.

17:56.070 --> 17:59.260
<i>This is obviously just a regular drugstore.</i>

17:59.940 --> 18:02.170
<i>Why did we go to one in the next town?</i>

18:02.860 --> 18:04.470
Hello.

18:05.030 --> 18:05.780
Oh.

18:06.700 --> 18:09.820
Thank goodness. 
I thought I had the wrong place.

18:09.820 --> 18:13.150
No, you didn't make a mistake. 
This is the place.

18:13.490 --> 18:15.680
Did you need to buy something?

18:15.680 --> 18:18.010
Yes. One sec.

18:19.610 --> 18:20.700
Excuse me.

18:20.700 --> 18:22.830
Yes? How can I help you?

18:22.830 --> 18:26.290
It's been a while. Do you remember me?

18:26.950 --> 18:27.500
Huh?

18:27.500 --> 18:29.650
You went to Higashi Elementary.

18:29.650 --> 18:33.460
When you were little, 
you would play near my mansion.

18:35.210 --> 18:39.140
O-Oh! The Adagaki place?

18:39.650 --> 18:41.930
Yes. I'm the only daughter of that family.

18:42.770 --> 18:43.530
And...

18:44.140 --> 18:46.100
you used to bully him.

18:53.020 --> 18:54.930
U-Um...

18:54.930 --> 18:56.230
You don't remember?

18:56.230 --> 19:01.950
Makabe Masamune. Back then, 
his name was Hayase Masamune.

19:02.650 --> 19:03.830
Hayase...

19:06.060 --> 19:07.660
Tubbymune?!

19:08.050 --> 19:10.870
Seriously? I didn't recognize you at all!

19:10.870 --> 19:13.020
Uh, yeah.

19:13.020 --> 19:14.670
You're like a totally different guy!

19:14.980 --> 19:18.180
Right? Because he lost an 
incredible amount of weight.

19:18.180 --> 19:20.690
Huh, I see.

19:22.980 --> 19:25.810
Hey, Suzuki-kun, are you 
done stocking the shelves?

19:26.090 --> 19:28.180
S-Sorry!

19:28.180 --> 19:31.650
Sorry to get in your way. 
Anyway, we'll be going now.

19:35.930 --> 19:37.070
Hayase-kun!

19:38.860 --> 19:40.900
Sorry about all that!

19:52.460 --> 19:54.060
Have you calmed down?

19:58.830 --> 20:01.380
Were you planning this from the start?

20:01.700 --> 20:04.650
Yes. How did you feel seeing him?

20:05.110 --> 20:06.350
Were you scared?

20:10.820 --> 20:16.290
No. Surprisingly, I felt fine.
Actually, it didn't even matter.

20:17.290 --> 20:20.740
<i>I thought I'd freak out a little more.</i>

20:21.250 --> 20:25.340
I found out where some of the others 
are now. Do you want to see them?

20:26.180 --> 20:27.200
Nah.

20:27.530 --> 20:30.190
I see. I figured.

20:31.100 --> 20:33.670
You're stronger now, Masamune.

20:36.940 --> 20:41.090
You worked really hard, you lost weight, 
and you were able to change.

20:43.170 --> 20:46.940
You're okay now. 
Have more confidence in yourself.

20:53.340 --> 20:56.750
Come on, stop that. Don't start 
crying after everything I just said.

20:57.490 --> 20:58.650
Sorry.

21:00.860 --> 21:03.860
Thank you, Aki-chan.

21:05.990 --> 21:08.780
Um, here.

21:09.190 --> 21:12.630
This isn't exactly to thank you 
for just now. It's for White Day.

21:13.510 --> 21:16.580
Really? What's inside?

21:16.580 --> 21:19.750
White chocolate. Sorry it's so unoriginal.

21:20.160 --> 21:22.710
The taste is more important than originality.

21:32.120 --> 21:36.660
<i>I want to touch her... I wonder if I can.</i>

21:44.420 --> 21:45.140
But...

21:46.290 --> 21:47.430
I'm sorry.

21:48.260 --> 21:50.150
I can't accept this.

21:53.090 --> 21:53.900
Huh?

21:55.330 --> 22:00.790
I think it's okay for at least one person to 
pick up what you're trying to throw away.

22:02.720 --> 22:03.960
So...

22:06.190 --> 22:09.410
Goodbye, Makabe Masamune-kun.
